# What must never enter a build context.
#
# The first two blocks are the important ones. A build context is uploaded to the daemon and
# every file in it can end up in a layer, so `.env` and `local/` being listed here is a safety
# property rather than an optimisation: the image is the thing that gets copied to a server.

# Secrets and the owner's own data
.env
.env.*
!env.example
local/
*.pem
*.key

# Git history — a 40 MB context for a 2 MB application, and a copy of every file ever committed
.git
.gitignore
.github

# The host's virtualenv: built for Windows, useless in a Linux image, and large
.venv
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache

# The frontend is built and served by Cloudflare, not by this image (ADR-001 §3)
frontend/

# Tests and docs do not run in production. They are read from the repository on the VM instead,
# so `docs/DEPLOY.md` is still at hand during a deploy.
tests/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Local tooling and scratch
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
uploads/
*.sqlite
*.db
leads.db
